---
alwaysApply: true
---

Next.js frontend rules:

- prefer server components unless client behavior is needed
- minimize client-side state
- avoid unnecessary useEffect usage
- fetch data efficiently
- keep components small and focused
- separate UI from business logic
- avoid prop drilling when possible
- reuse shared UI patterns
- nest files in folders if files are not related to outher external files.

Performance:

- optimize images
- avoid unnecessary rerenders
- lazy load heavy components
- avoid large client bundles

UI:

- maintain consistent spacing and design patterns
- make components reusable only when justified
- avoid overly generic components
